{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Spend pause engaged — 2026-09-17\n\nThe Bedrock daily spend warning is active. Recording the pause here, since this ticket owns the pause-until-next-day guidance.\n\n**Detection.** SSM `/bedrock-spend-cap/state` now carries `warned_day: 2026-09-17`, which was not present at the previous poll this session. The `bedrock-spend-cap` Lambda's own log line confirms the live metered value has crossed the configured warning threshold and is tracking toward the hard deny threshold, with `attached=False` (the deny policy has not been applied).\n\n**`ce_spend` is not the signal to read.** It reports `0.0` for today. Cost Explorer lags by up to 24 hours, so early in a day it reads zero regardless of actual usage. The Lambda's `metered` value is the live figure and is what drives both thresholds. Any future automation that polls this parameter must compare against `metered`, not `ce_spend` — a `ce_spend`-based guard would have failed to detect today's warning entirely. This corrects the detection approach recorded earlier in this ticket.\n\n**Scope of the pause.** Suspended until after midnight local:\n\n- `review_plan_start` and `verify_completion_start`\n- ticket closes, because the completion gate is itself a billable LLM op\n- pushes to Gerrit, because a new patchset triggers the Bedrock-backed review bot\n\nContinuing, because none of it draws on the Bedrock account:\n\n- tracker reads and writes\n- CloudWatch and GitHub Actions monitoring\n- background investigation agents already running, which execute on the harness model\n\n**Resume condition.** After 2026-09-18 00:00 local, when the daily counter rolls over. The orchestrator loop checks the pause state on every tick and clears it automatically once that time passes.\n\n**A confounder worth knowing before trusting the number.** The Lambda cannot price the model family that rebar's LLM operations actually use, and is falling back to a synthetic rate for all of it. That is tracked as a separate bug. The pause is being honoured regardless — a fail-closed estimate is the safe direction to be wrong in — but the accuracy of the figure that triggered it is genuinely in question.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789672154216737154,"uuid":"62fe454b-1697-4a3f-af86-9defe913035c"}